// DejaVu Sans Bold, subsetted to Latin-1, Greek, arrows and the mathematical
// operator blocks — about 130 kB of font for roughly 3 kB of symbols a school
// paper actually uses.
//
// jsPDF's built-in fonts are WinAnsi-encoded, so "√" and "≠" came out as
// mangled punctuation. Embedding a real Unicode font is what lets the
// downloaded PDF print the symbol a teacher typed. It lives in the lazily
// imported PDF chunk, so nobody who never downloads a paper pays for it.
//
// Arabic script is deliberately not in the subset: jsPDF cannot do the
// contextual shaping or right-to-left layout Urdu needs, so a font alone
// would not have produced readable Urdu. Those papers go through Print.
export const PDF_UNICODE_FONT_BASE64 =
  ''
